From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: servicemanager and SurfaceFlinger as shared libraries

Appends libapklayer_servicemanager and libapklayer_surfaceflinger: the binaries' own sources as shared
libraries exporting main, because bionic_translation loads libraries, not executables (PLAN P7.1,
docs/AOSP-BUILDS.md). This was a hand edit with no script before. The tree also has an empty
services/surfaceflinger/include/ (a patch cannot carry an empty directory; no Android.bp or .mk in
frameworks/native, vendor/apklayer or build/soong names it, so it is left out; if Soong ever asks for it,
`mkdir -p services/surfaceflinger/include`).
Against frameworks/native 46018f54b424 (REVISION). Apply: patches/apply aosp <LineageOS tree>.
---
diff --git a/cmds/servicemanager/Android.bp b/cmds/servicemanager/Android.bp
index e5d7b7456b..955ba96736 100644
--- a/cmds/servicemanager/Android.bp
+++ b/cmds/servicemanager/Android.bp
@@ -130,3 +130,31 @@ cc_fuzz {
         ],
     },
 }
+
+// apklayer: the service manager as a library (its main() is exported) so a launcher on bionic_translation can run it. The tree's
+// ServiceManager and main are used as they are; the access policy (SELinux) is replaced by vendor/apklayer's allow-all Access.
+cc_library_shared {
+    name: "libapklayer_servicemanager",
+    srcs: [
+        "main.cpp",
+        "ServiceManager.cpp",
+        ":apklayer_servicemanager_access",
+    ],
+    compile_multilib: "64",
+    cflags: [
+        "-Wall",
+        "-Wextra",
+        "-Werror",
+        "-DANDROID_UTILS_REF_BASE_DISABLE_IMPLICIT_CONSTRUCTION",
+        "-Wno-unused-private-field",  // Access.h declares the SELinux context our allow-all Access does not use
+    ],
+    shared_libs: [
+        "libbase",
+        "libvintf",
+        "libcutils",
+        "liblog",
+        "libutils",
+        "libperfetto_c",
+        "libbinder",
+    ],
+}
diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/Android.bp b/services/surfaceflinger/Android.bp
index f69e5bc1ab..09aa870a6d 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/Android.bp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/Android.bp
@@ -491,3 +491,16 @@ genrule {
         "statslog_surfaceflinger.cpp",
     ],
 }
+
+// apklayer: SurfaceFlinger as a library (its main() is exported) so a launcher on bionic_translation can run it
+cc_library_shared {
+    name: "libapklayer_surfaceflinger",
+    defaults: ["libsurfaceflinger_binary"],
+    srcs: [
+        ":surfaceflinger_binary_sources",
+        "SurfaceFlingerFactory.cpp",
+    ],
+    shared_libs: ["libSurfaceFlingerProp"],
+    allow_undefined_symbols: true, // Layer::logFrameStats is declared and never defined (dead code in the binary)
+    logtags: ["surfaceflinger.logtags"],
+}
